(*
expect:
stale-handle probe done
*)
(* Does a REGISTRATION destroy an already-queued timer event? (#151 probe 2)

   The suspected loss path, all three steps in `nodus/tuvm/src/backend/zephyr/`:

     1. timer_zephyr.c:38   one-shot A expires in ISR -> pulse_post_isr(sys/timer, H)
     2. timer_zephyr.c:56   ANY later registration calls reap_oneshots() first, which
                            sees A has fired and does handle_free(H); handle_new may
                            then hand H straight back to the new timer
     3. pulse_zephyr.c:76   the pump does handle_get(H), gets NULL for the stale
                            generation, and discards the item — with NO counter

   A's event is gone. Nothing is dropped, nothing is coalesced, nothing is logged.

   This is the shape ShipsBellAlarmNodeC6 executes at every boundary inside ONE
   reaction: strikeOn arms the 10 ms stroke, `out` writes a line (UART, and since
   #56 a UDP datagram too), then armAfter: registers the alarm and the watchdog.
   If the stroke expires before those registrations run, its event is destroyed and
   strokeStep never fires — so `pinOn` stays true and `striking` latches, which is a
   piezo held ON with no later boundary able to recover it.

   THE A/B. Both arms arm a one-shot and then burn past its expiry inside the same
   reaction. They differ in ONE line: arm B registers another timer afterwards, arm
   A does not. If the control delivers and the test does not, the registration is
   the destroyer and nothing else can be.

   Reading it: "control delivered 1 / test delivered 0" confirms. Both 1 refutes —
   say so and stop. Both 0 means the burn itself broke delivery and the probe is
   invalid, not the theory.

   Holds ONE Timers instance. Never returns from a phase with a live repeater —
   there are none here, only one-shots. Dialect: `[ ... ] whileTrue:`, no modulo. *)
class StaleHandleProbeC6 packageUsing: manifest = (
  | plat space timers lostCh kickCh beatCh beats ::= 0.
    delivered ::= 0. kicks ::= 0. armDecoy ::= false. |
) (

  public main: platform args: args = (
    plat:: platform.
    space:: plat space.
    timers:: plat timers.
    space whenever: 'sys/timer' do: [ :e | timers dispatch: e ].

    lostCh:: space channel: 'probe/lost'.
    lostCh whenever: '' do: [ :m | delivered:: delivered + 1 ].

    kickCh:: space channel: 'probe/kick'.
    kickCh whenever: '' do: [ :m | self onKick ].

    beatCh:: space channel: 'probe/beat'.
    beatCh whenever: '' do: [ :m | beats:: beats + 1 ].

    'stale-handle probe: A/B on one line of difference' out.

    (* The heartbeat. pumpEvents BLOCKS K_FOREVER on an empty mailbox, so without a
       standing wake source the control arm parks and proves nothing (it did, first
       run). A REPEATER is the only safe choice: reap_oneshots() frees `live &&
       !repeating` entries only, and it runs on REGISTRATION, never on expiry — so a
       repeater armed here, once, before anything else exists, keeps the pump turning
       for the rest of the run without ever reaping. Registering it up front also
       keeps it out of both arms, so the A/B still differs by exactly one line. *)
    timers every: 25 post: #h on: beatCh.

    self runArm: 'control (no registration after)' decoy: false.
    self runArm: 'test    (registration after)   ' decoy: true.

    'stale-handle probe done' out.
  )

  (* One arm. The kick handler does the whole sequence inside a single reaction,
     which is the only place this race can be built. *)
  runArm: label decoy: wantDecoy = (
    | spins |
    delivered:: 0. kicks:: 0. armDecoy:: wantDecoy.
    timers after: 5 post: #k on: kickCh.

    (* Drain for a bounded number of turns rather than until delivery: waiting for
       an event that is the thing under test would hang forever when the test
       arm behaves as predicted. pumpEvents BLOCKS on an empty mailbox, so the
       decoy one-shot below is also what guarantees this loop can still turn. *)
    spins:: beats + 40.                  (* ~1 s of heartbeats *)
    [ beats < spins ] whileTrue: [
      plat pumpEvents. space drain ].

    (label , ': delivered ' , delivered printString) out.
    ^ self )

  onKick = (
    kicks:: kicks + 1.
    kicks > 1 ifTrue: [ ^ self ].        (* the decoy re-entry does nothing *)

    (* 1. arm the "stroke" *)
    timers after: 10 post: #l on: lostCh.

    (* 2. still inside this reaction, burn past its 10 ms expiry so its post is
          sitting in the mailbox, exactly as `out` does in the real striker *)
    self burn: 60.

    (* 3. THE ONE LINE OF DIFFERENCE. A registration here runs reap_oneshots(),
          which frees the handle the queued post still refers to. *)
    armDecoy ifTrue: [ timers after: 400 post: #k on: kickCh ].

    ^ self )

  burn: ms = (
    | until |
    until:: plat monotonicMillis + ms.
    [ plat monotonicMillis < until ] whileTrue: [ ].
    ^ self )

) : (
)
